    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.10951443199350053,
        "y0": 0.4635992933622165,
        "x1": 0.8907501733603598,
        "y1": 0.47655546863401865
      },
      "text": "Motivated by the action of time-variables and Virasoro operators on SIB polynomials that we dis-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1095144063484769,
        "y0": 0.48255440628160495,
        "x1": 0.8905213941045168,
        "y1": 0.4955105815534071
      },
      "text": "cuss in this section it is instructive to slightly change notation of diagrams DP - distinct partitions.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1095144063484769,
        "y0": 0.5015095192009933,
        "x1": 0.8905697093290441,
        "y1": 0.5144656944727954
      },
      "text": "For this purpose we represent a Young diagram (turned upside down) as a way of tight packing",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1095144063484769,
        "y0": 0.5204641609463725,
        "x1": 0.4212856773568803,
        "y1": 0.5334203362181748
      },
      "text": "of square boxes in a corner of a room.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.43295857405462185,
        "y0": 0.5204641609463725,
        "x1": 0.8905849937631303,
        "y1": 0.5334203362181748
      },
      "text": "In this setting distinct partitions (DP) are in one-to-one",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1095144063484769,
        "y0": 0.5392767618500989,
        "x1": 0.8905517578125,
        "y1": 0.552232937121901
      },
      "text": "correspondence with possible ways of tight packing of square boxes under a ladder. We demonstrate",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1095144063484769,
        "y0": 0.5582314035954781,
        "x1": 0.8905239586068803,
        "y1": 0.5711875788672802
      },
      "text": "examples of these diagrams, left picture correspond to usual Young diagram, right one correspond",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1095144063484769,
        "y0": 0.5771865165148664,
        "x1": 0.2724263167180935,
        "y1": 0.5901426917866687
      },
      "text": "to distinct partition:",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19109916366448923,
        "y0": 0.8155842008613351,
        "x1": 0.21433064436712185,
        "y1": 0.8285403761331372
      },
      "text": "(a)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.22660081366530987,
        "y0": 0.8155842008613351,
        "x1": 0.34736220415900737,
        "y1": 0.8285403761331372
      },
      "text": "Usual partition",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
